      "description": "Full SS-5 sweet spot session. 4 intervals of 10 minutes at 94% FTP (188W), with 5 min Z1 recovery between each. 40 minutes total time-in-zone. Upper sweet spot / low Z4 territory. Standard WU and CD. ~85 min total. Target HR: 140-150 bpm during intervals.\n\nWarmup\n- Easy start. Gradual ramp over 5 minutes. Cadence 85-95 rpm. 240^ Almost at Z2. Let the power build naturally.<!> 5m ramp 25-65%\n\n- 5 minutes steady Z2. Settle your breathing. HR comfortable and low. 240^ Z3 activations coming. One minute.<!> 5m 65%\n- Z3 activation - 1 minute. Wake the legs up.<!> 1m 78%\n- Easy spin. One more activation coming.<!> 1m 50%\n- Second activation. Last step before sweet spot.<!> 1m 78%\n- 30-second primer at 188W. Feel the zone before the main set.<!> 30s 94%\n- Settle. 2 minutes. Four blocks of 10 minutes at 188W. Upper sweet spot - this is proper work. 90^ 30 seconds. Ready?<!> 2m 50%\n- Interval 1 - 10 minutes at 188W. Controlled start - don't sprint off the line. 120^ 2 minutes in. HR rising. Target 140-150 bpm across all intervals. 300^ Halfway. Power steady. Let HR stabilise. 480^ 2 minutes left. Hold the line. 570^ 30 seconds. Finish clean.<!> 10m 94%\n- Recovery - 5 minutes. Keep pedalling. HR should drop back below 125 bpm. 240^ 1 minute to go. Interval 2 is identical to interval 1.<!> 5m 50%\n- Interval 2 - 10 minutes. Match the power from interval 1. Consistent is the goal. 120^ 2 minutes in. Rhythm established. 300^ Halfway. HR stable in the 140-150 bpm band? 480^ 2 minutes left. Power holding? 570^ 30 seconds.<!> 10m 94%\n- Recovery - 5 minutes. Two down, two to go. 240^ 1 minute. Interval 3 - same again.<!> 5m 50%\n- Interval 3 - 10 minutes. Third block. Fatigue is starting to show now. 120^ 2 minutes in. If HR is above 152 bpm, ease back 5W - don't push into threshold zone. 300^ Halfway. Power consistency across all three blocks is what matters. 480^ 2 minutes left. One more block after this. 570^ 30 seconds.<!> 10m 94%\n- Recovery - 5 minutes. Last one. 10 minutes at 188W. 240^ 1 minute. Final interval. Go get it.<!> 5m 50%\n- Interval 4 - 10 minutes. The fourth block. This is where this week is harder than last week. 120^ 2 minutes in. Hold the line. 300^ Halfway. Power drop vs interval 1? Under 5W is excellent. Over 10W - note it, that's your current ceiling. 420^ 3 minutes left. Don't let it slip. 480^ 2 minutes. Dig. 570^ 30 seconds. Everything left.<!> 10m 94%\n\nCooldown\n- Done. 10 minutes cool-down. 40 minutes of upper sweet spot in the legs. Good work. 300^ Halfway. Cadence easy. Let everything settle. 570^ Almost done.<!> 10m ramp 65-25%\n\n",
